{"content":"💡 **SUGGESTION: reset `_jobBoardPersistedLiveIds` before the empty-ledger early return**

`_rehydrateJobBoard` resets the throttle **before** the early return, with an explicit invariant comment:

```dart
// gh-1590: the persist window opens with the (re)hydrated session —
// BEFORE the empty-ledger early return, so a session switch never
// inherits the previous session's window.
_jobBoardPersistThrottle.reset();
final latest = ShellJobBoard.latestRecords(await session.getEntries());
if (latest.isEmpty) return;          // <-- early return
...
_jobBoardPersistDeduper.reset();     // <-- only reached when non-empty
_jobBoardPersistedLiveIds = null;    // line 539: same conditional path
```

When a session switch lands on a session with **no** `shell_job_registry` records (a jobs-less session after a jobs-carrying one), `_jobBoardPersistedLiveIds` keeps the previous session's live ids — the exact "inherits the previous session" situation the throttle reset's comment rules out. (The deduper has the same pre-existing placement, so this follows an existing pattern.)

Impact is benign **fail-open**: stale ids can only make `grewLive` *more* likely to fire (an extra append), never suppress a crash-critical start append — the fix's invariant still holds. But for symmetry with the throttle's documented guarantee, move the reset up:

```dart
_jobBoardPersistThrottle.reset();
_jobBoardPersistedLiveIds = null;
final latest = ShellJobBoard.latestRecords(await session.getEntries());
if (latest.isEmpty) return;
```

(If you also consider the deduper reset misplaced, that's a pre-existing gh-1073 concern and would deserve its own issue rather than riding this PR.)
